# Kodi Python API Reference

## xbmcplugin -- Plugin Directory Management

```python
import xbmcplugin

xbmcplugin.addDirectoryItems(handle, [(url, listitem, is_folder), ...], totalItems)
xbmcplugin.setContent(handle, 'videos')  # or 'movies', 'tvshows', 'episodes', 'musicvideos'
xbmcplugin.endOfDirectory(handle, succeeded=True, updateListing=False, cacheToDisc=True)
xbmcplugin.setResolvedUrl(handle, succeeded=True, listitem=play_item)
xbmcplugin.addSortMethod(handle, xbmcplugin.SORT_METHOD_UNSORTED)
xbmcplugin.setProperty(handle, key, value)
xbmcplugin.setPluginCategory(handle, category_name)
```

- `handle` is always `int(sys.argv[1])` -- the integer passed by Kodi to the plugin.
- Always call `endOfDirectory()` after adding items, or Kodi shows an error.
- For playback, items must have `listitem.setProperty("IsPlayable", "true")`.

## xbmcgui -- UI Elements

```python
from xbmcgui import ListItem, Dialog, Window

li = ListItem(label='Title', offscreen=True)
li.setArt({'poster': url, 'fanart': url, 'icon': url, 'thumb': url})
li.setProperty('IsPlayable', 'true')

info_tag = li.getVideoInfoTag()
info_tag.setTitle('Title')
info_tag.setMediaType('movie')  # 'movie', 'tvshow', 'season', 'episode'
info_tag.setYear(2024)
info_tag.setPlot('Description text')
info_tag.setGenres(['Action', 'Drama'])

dialog = Dialog()
dialog.ok('Header', 'Message')
result = dialog.yesno('Header', 'Question?')
dialog.notification('Header', 'Message', xbmcgui.NOTIFICATION_INFO, 3000)
```

- Prefer `offscreen=True` when creating ListItems that won't be immediately displayed (performance).
- Use `getVideoInfoTag()` / `InfoTagVideo` instead of the deprecated `setInfo()` for Kodi 20+.
- This codebase uses `script.module.infotagger` to handle metadata tagging.

## xbmcaddon -- Addon Configuration

```python
import xbmcaddon

addon = xbmcaddon.Addon()
addon = xbmcaddon.Addon('plugin.video.themoviedb.helper')

value = addon.getSetting('setting_id')       # always returns string
addon.setSetting('setting_id', 'value')      # value must be string
path = addon.getAddonInfo('path')            # addon install directory
addon_id = addon.getAddonInfo('id')
version = addon.getAddonInfo('version')
localized = addon.getLocalizedString(32000)  # from strings.po
```

- `getSetting()` always returns a string. Cast to `int`, `bool`, etc. as needed.
- In this codebase, use `get_setting()` from `tmdbhelper.lib.addon.plugin` instead of raw `Addon().getSetting()`.

## xbmcvfs -- File System

```python
import xbmcvfs

real_path = xbmcvfs.translatePath('special://profile/addon_data/plugin.video.themoviedb.helper/')
exists = xbmcvfs.exists(path)          # works with special:// paths
xbmcvfs.mkdirs(path)                   # create directory tree
dirs, files = xbmcvfs.listdir(path)

f = xbmcvfs.File(path, 'r')
content = f.read()
f.close()

xbmcvfs.delete(path)
xbmcvfs.rmdir(path)
```

- Use `xbmcvfs` for all file operations instead of `os` / `open()` when working with `special://` paths.
- `translatePath()` converts `special://` to OS paths -- only needed for `os.path` or stdlib calls.

## xbmc -- Core Functions

```python
import xbmc

xbmc.log('Message', xbmc.LOGDEBUG)      # LOGDEBUG, LOGINFO, LOGWARNING, LOGERROR
xbmc.executebuiltin('Container.Refresh')
xbmc.executebuiltin('RunScript(plugin.video.themoviedb.helper,action=value)')
xbmc.getCondVisibility('Window.IsActive(home)')  # returns bool
xbmc.getInfoLabel('System.BuildVersion')
xbmc.sleep(1000)                         # milliseconds, use sparingly

monitor = xbmc.Monitor()
monitor.waitForAbort(timeout)            # preferred over xbmc.sleep for services
player = xbmc.Player()
```

- Never use `print()` for output. Always use `xbmc.log()` or the addon's `kodi_log()` wrapper.
- In services, use `monitor.waitForAbort()` instead of `xbmc.sleep()` to respect Kodi shutdown.
- `executebuiltin()` runs Kodi built-in functions (Container.Refresh, Notification, ActivateWindow, etc.).

## Lazy Imports Pattern

This codebase deliberately uses lazy imports (importing inside functions) to minimize plugin startup time:

```python
def some_function():
    from xbmcgui import Dialog
    Dialog().ok('Title', 'Message')
```

Follow this pattern for all Kodi module imports inside handler functions. Top-level imports are reserved for lightweight, always-needed modules.
